 "title": "43/19 = [2; 3, 1, 4] as squares",
 "caption": "Tile a 43 × 19 rectangle with the biggest squares possible: 2 squares of side 19, then 3 of side 5, then 1 of side 4, then 4 of side 1. Those counts, 2, 3, 1, 4, are the continued fraction [2; 3, 1, 4].",
 "alt": "A rectangle 43 by 19 tiled by two 19 squares, three 5 squares, one 4 square and four unit squares.",
 "description": [
  "Take a rectangle 43 wide and 19 tall.",
  "Two squares of side 19 fit (43 = 2 × 19 + 5), leaving a 5 × 19 strip.",
  "Three squares of side 5 fit (19 = 3 × 5 + 4), leaving a 5 × 4 piece.",
  "One square of side 4 fits (5 = 1 × 4 + 1), leaving a 1 × 4 piece.",
  "Four unit squares finish it (4 = 4 × 1), so 43/19 = [2; 3, 1, 4]."
 ],
